---
const stats = [
  { n: 'Up to 40%', d: 'of new dental patients never return after their first visit, not because of the dentistry, but because nobody followed up.' },
  { n: '$146K', d: 'of revenue a typical practice quietly loses every year to churn, missed recalls, and forgotten aftercare.' },
  { n: '1 in 3', d: 'patients say they would refer a friend, but almost nobody ever asks, and there is no easy way to reward it.' },
]
---
<section id="problem" class="scroll-mt-24 bg-cream-100 py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 sm:px-8">
    <p class="text-center text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-teal-700">The gap nobody owns</p>
    <h2 class="mt-4 text-center font-heading text-[clamp(1.9rem,3.6vw,3rem)] font-semibold leading-[1.06] tracking-tight text-ink-900 text-balance">
      The visit ends. The relationship shouldn't.
    </h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-2xl text-center text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
      The most valuable moment in dentistry is the week after treatment, when a patient is most grateful and most likely to tell a friend. It's also the week most practices leave to chance.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-cream-300 bg-cream-300 sm:grid-cols-3">
      {stats.map((s) => (
        <div class="bg-cream-50 p-8">
          <p class="font-heading text-[clamp(2.2rem,4vw,3rem)] font-semibold leading-none text-ink-900">{s.n}</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-600">{s.d}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-center text-xs text-ink-400">Industry benchmarks and patient surveys for US dental practices.</p>
  </div>
</section>
